      "conclusion": "Suspected septic arthritis after an intra-articular injection: no acupuncture, emergency referral the same day.",
      "keyReasoning": [
        "Fever, a hot swollen joint and inability to bear weight after a joint injection are red flags for septic arthritis.",
        "Needling near a possibly infected joint is contraindicated; delay risks joint destruction and sepsis."
      ],
      "teachingPoints": [
        "Screen every painful joint for heat, swelling, fever and recent procedures before needling.",
        "Refer to the Emergency Department the same day; do not offer a routine appointment."
      ]
